.TH "Docv::CrystalPages::Types" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::CrystalPages::Types \- Lookup tables over the documented types.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::CrystalPages::Types\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Lookup tables over the documented types.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.PP
\fBCODE_SPAN = /(?<!\(ga)(\(ga+)(?!\(ga)(.+?)(?<!\(ga)\e1(?!\(ga)/m\fR
.PP
\fBTYPE_PATH = /\eA((?:::)?[A\-Z]\ew*(?:::[A\-Z]\ew*)*)(?:[#.(]|\ez)/\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(project : Project)\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef []?(full_name : String) : TypeDoc | Nil\fR
The documented type named \fIfull_name\fR, generic arguments ignored.
.TP 4
\fBdef lookup(context : TypeDoc, name : String) : TypeDoc | Nil\fR
Resolves \fIname\fR as Crystal does: relative to \fIcontext\fR, then to each
enclosing namespace.
.PP
\fBdef project : Project\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef referenced(type : TypeDoc) : Array(TypeDoc)\fR
Types the docs of \fItype\fR name in code spans: \fB\%Tree\fR, \fB\%Tree#edit\fR,
\fB\%Language.load\fR, \fB\%Language::MIN_ABI\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef types : Array(Docv::CrystalPages::TypeDoc)\fR
The types with a page of their own: the top level when it declares
anything, then every type in nesting order.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/crystal_pages/model.cr
